{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "New Challenges"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Page Layout"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le09ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reservations"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "doubts or \u200breasons for not \u200baccepting or \u200bagreeing with something \u200bcompletely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Denise and I have some reservations with the illustrations."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le09ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a workplace environment."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "concerns"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bworried \u200bfeeling, or a \u200bstate of \u200banxiety"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What are your concerns?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le09ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to concur"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to agree"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do you concur?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le09ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to monopolize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have or take \u200bcomplete \u200bcontrol of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think it's a little too aggressive for our liking, plus it monopolizes too much space."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le09ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sign-off on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to officially approve something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you sign-off on it we can go from there."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le09ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reiterate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say something again"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As I reiterated before, we ought to have more balance on the page."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le09ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect: Commenting on the Present Results of Something in the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about events that happened in the past with a connection to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the Present Perfect tense is: <br/>subject + has/have + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to comment on past events that have a present connection, you can use the words <span class=\"italic\">appear</span>, <span class=\"italic\">seem</span> and <span class=\"italic\">sound</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">appears</span> I<span class=\"strong\">'ve been stressed</span> for no reason! The project isn't due until next month! <br/>It <span class=\"strong\">seems</span> they<span class=\"strong\">'ve decided</span> to postpone the deadline. <br/>You <span class=\"strong\">sound</span> as though you<span class=\"strong\">'ve become</span> fed up with the current situation at work.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't know if we've ever met before, I'm Kristi."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've felt since we saw the illustrations that they appear to be too busy. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've seen other book titles incorporate that look and it seems to be more kid-friendly."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I got a great font that I've wanted to use, but haven't had a chance."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Denise has prefered it in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've wanted to make this book more kid-friendly since we've gotten involved with this project."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Expressing Duty and Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> to talk about duty and advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to say what the right thing to do is or the best thing to do is, you can use the modals <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> and their Perfect forms <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to have</span>. You use the Perfect forms to refer to duties and advice for past situations. <span class=\"italic\">Should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> are not as strong as <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, but are more appropriate in formal situations, like in the workplace."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">should</span> prepare for the presentation this afternoon. We won't have time otherwise. <br/>You <span class=\"strong\">should</span> always be present at the morning meetings. <br/>They <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span> give money to charities - it helps to market the brand. <br/>Who <span class=\"strong\">should</span> we include in the memo?</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've also felt that typeface ought to be changed."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We think the letters should have simple, generous letter shapes. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "As I reiterated before, we ought to have more balance on the page."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Should it be kind of like old English style or should it be closer to Comic Sans?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a letter to a friend who is visiting your city or country next month."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You will not be there when your friend visits so you need to give him/ her information that you think tourists should know about, like the currency, nightlife, places to go sightseeing and so on."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include information about what visitors should do as well, especially when it comes to social customs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include a friendly greeting and appropriate closing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give your letter to one of your classmates to read."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a letter to my friend who is going to visit my city or country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give my friend some advice for his/her trip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read a letter from one of my classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can discuss reasons and results of an event or action related to work and jobs."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can express duty and advice related to work and job issues."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can exchange complex professional information related to work and job issues."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you consider yourself artistic? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " How do you deal with constructive criticism?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "I'm afraid we are on different