e": 1}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn11le09ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Thanks for coming in. I don't know if we've ever met before, I'm Kristi.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: No, first time. I'm Ronald.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Nice to meet you Ronald. Now, as I mentioned, Denise and I have some reservations with the illustrations.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>:  Ok. What are your concerns?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Well first, we've felt since we saw the illustrations that they appear to be too busy. From my perspective, the illustrations should have more balance between the visuals and the white space on the page. Do you concur?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: Um. Yes, We can do that for you.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le09ob06re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "32500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>:  Excellent. Next, we also thought that the font size ought to be increased from 20 to 24 and that the typeface ought to be changed. Then, we think the letters should have simple, generous letter shapes. I've seen other book titles incorporate that look and it seems to be more kid-friendly. Right now it looks a little too corporate.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: Should it be kind of like old English style or should it be closer to Comic Sans?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Closer to Comic Sans.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: I got a great font and I've wanted to use, but haven't had a chance. Perhaps I can try it out and send the design to you? If you sign-off on it we can go from there.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le09ob06re2img06.jpg"}, {"time": "70000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Sure no problem. Finally, we ought to avoid using all caps if we can on this page here.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: Are you sure? Denise has preferred it in the past. It's easier to see and makes a bold statement on the page?\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: She identified it as a concern herself. I think it's a little too aggressive for our liking, plus it monopolizes too much space. As I reiterated before, we ought to have more balance on the page.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: Ok. That makes sense.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: All right. I think that's all I have. Thank you for coming in and as I said before, we've wanted to make this book more kid-friendly since we've gotten involved with this project. Maybe just keep that in mind. If you have any questions or need to check anything, just let me know.\n<br/><span class=\"strong\">Ronald</span>: I'll be in touch.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le09ob06re2img07.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le09ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le09ob06re2img01.jpg"}}], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}